1
00:00:02,830 --> 00:00:04,620
Okay, guys, listen.

2
00:00:04,870 --> 00:00:07,380
Tomorrow, Emily gets married again.

3
00:00:07,630 --> 00:00:10,420
So try to really keep Ross' mind off of it.

4
00:00:10,590 --> 00:00:12,050
- Okay.     - Good idea.

5
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,800
Hey, man. What's up?

6
00:00:15,090 --> 00:00:17,800
Just thinking about Emily getting married tomorrow.

7
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:22,980
Oh, Ross. Look, look.

8
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:25,440
What? Where?

9
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,190
Right over there. There. Look, look, look.

10
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:32,530
- What am I looking at?     - Somebody help me out here.

11
00:00:33,530 --> 00:00:36,030
- Hey.     - Hey.

12
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:39,160
Monica, sorry I didn't come by. I was out with Gary.

13
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:43,830
He let me ride around with him. We saw and prevented crimes.

14
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:46,170
- You got to go on a ride-along?     - Uh-huh.

15
00:00:46,370 --> 00:00:48,830
- I want to go on a ride-along.     - Me too.

16
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:50,710
- Okay.     - Yeah. Me too.

17
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,670
Really? You?

18
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:56,470
Yeah.

19
00:00:57,050 --> 00:01:00,510
- Well, it's kind of dangerous.     - Well, I like danger.

20
00:01:00,890 --> 00:01:03,890
- Okay, you guys free tonight?     - Yeah.

21
00:01:04,730 --> 00:01:07,600
You didn't say it was gonna be at nighttime.

22
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:02,620
- Hey.    - Hey.

23
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:05,620
I'm glad you're home. We can finally organize these photos.

24
00:02:05,830 --> 00:02:07,830
Oh, thank God.

25
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:10,170
Finally.

26
00:02:10,670 --> 00:02:13,090
I've broken them down into categories.

27
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:16,170
We got holidays, birthdays, candids...

28
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:18,760
And I've cross-referenced them by subject.

29
00:02:18,970 --> 00:02:21,010
So if you're looking up, say...

30
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:24,140
...birthdays and dogs, you get photo 152.

31
00:02:24,390 --> 00:02:25,430
See?

32
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:29,230
Oh, it's me and LePoo.

33
00:02:29,810 --> 00:02:31,730
Wow, I miss that dog.

34
00:02:31,980 --> 00:02:34,900
You can also find him under "dog" and "dead."

35
00:02:37,190 --> 00:02:38,190
Great. Thanks.

36
00:02:38,900 --> 00:02:42,240
Hand me that other box of photos. That's the last one.

37
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:49,660
Oops.

38
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:51,170
Sorry.

39
00:02:51,370 --> 00:02:53,210
Good thing you numbered them.

40
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:54,460
I hadn't.

41
00:02:54,630 --> 00:02:57,420
Photo 152 was a prototype.

42
00:02:58,970 --> 00:03:01,050
Honey, it's okay. It's okay.

43
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:04,470
How about I fix you a drink? Maybe a margarita?

44
00:03:04,970 --> 00:03:06,510
Ross has the blender.

45
00:03:06,930 --> 00:03:10,100
Everything's just falling apart.

46
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:13,850
It's okay. I'll go to Ross', get the blender.

47
00:03:14,110 --> 00:03:16,570
- You get the margarita stuff ready.     - All right.

48
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:19,650
His keys are in the drawer. Also, I need some cash.

49
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:21,240
Want me to stop at the ATM?

50
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:24,780
No. While you're at Ross', if you see any lying around.

51
00:03:26,830 --> 00:03:28,660
- What?     - What?

52
00:03:28,830 --> 00:03:30,830
I don't do that.

53
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:44,550
That was so cool, man. The way you leaned on that guy.

54
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:47,300
It is starting to get dark out there.

55
00:03:47,970 --> 00:03:50,640
He told you everything. You cracked him.

56
00:03:50,890 --> 00:03:54,140
He was the victim. They're usually pretty talkative.

57
00:03:54,850 --> 00:03:57,940
Okay, but it is officially nighttime.

58
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:02,530
- Want me to grab the berry?     - It's called a cherry.

59
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:05,160
It's called... Chandler.

60
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:12,290
Okay, I got it.

61
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:15,790
This place makes the best sandwich in the world.

62
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,750
Does it have meatballs?

63
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:18,960
Oh, yeah.

64
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:20,800
Melted cheese and marinara sauce?

65
00:04:21,090 --> 00:04:22,300
Yep.

66
00:04:22,470 --> 00:04:24,260
You can't eat that in my car.

67
00:04:26,550 --> 00:04:28,300
Yeah, okay.

68
00:04:28,470 --> 00:04:31,720
Even though my tax dollars paid for this car.

69
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:34,600
Your tax dollars?

70
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:38,770
Yeah, okay.

71
00:04:45,450 --> 00:04:47,450
Wow, that sandwich smells good.

72
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:49,570
Did I say you could smell it?

73
00:04:50,660 --> 00:04:51,910
I can't smell it?

74
00:04:52,330 --> 00:04:56,710
Half the taste is in the smell. You're sucking up all the taste units.

75
00:04:57,250 --> 00:04:58,880
Okay, I'll give them back.

76
00:05:02,590 --> 00:05:04,300
What is so great about that sandwich?

77
00:05:05,300 --> 00:05:09,510
- Okay. Imagine the best sex you ever had.     - Okay.

78
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:11,970
- Are you thinking about Monica?     - Yeah.

79
00:05:12,310 --> 00:05:13,350
What's that like?

80
00:05:26,650 --> 00:05:29,820
Please don't be from a real dinosaur. Please, please.

81
00:05:30,070 --> 00:05:33,660
Please, please, please.

82
00:05:33,830 --> 00:05:36,160
"Made in Mexico." Yes!

83
00:05:38,290 --> 00:05:40,420
Who would buy this?

84
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:49,550
Rach, it's me. Pick up.

85
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:53,260
What's up?

86
00:05:53,470 --> 00:05:55,430
I need more margarita things.

87
00:05:55,680 --> 00:06:00,810
I need some salt, some margarita mix and tequila.

88
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:03,770
So all we had was ice?

89
00:06:04,150 --> 00:06:05,530
See if he has ice.

90
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:07,740
Okay.

91
00:06:19,620 --> 00:06:20,750
Hello, Ross?

92
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:22,290
It's Emily here.

93
00:06:22,540 --> 00:06:26,630
I know this is out of the blue, but I'm getting married tomorrow.

94
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:28,760
Well, maybe I am...

95
00:06:29,010 --> 00:06:30,970
I keep thinking about you.

96
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:35,390
And I'm wondering if we made a mistake giving up so fast.

97
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:37,560
Are you thinking about me?

98
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:41,230
No, of course you're not. But if you are, call me tonight.

99
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:43,110
Okay, bye.

100
00:06:52,410 --> 00:06:53,410
Where we going?

101
00:06:53,570 --> 00:06:56,910
This witness won't return my calls. We'll surprise him coming home.

102
00:06:57,120 --> 00:07:00,750
Surprise him? We're not gonna make anybody mad, are we?

103
00:07:01,250 --> 00:07:02,830
Come on, man.

104
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:07,340
You gonna squeeze the perp's shoes a bit before he lawyers up?

105
00:07:07,590 --> 00:07:10,170
He's a witness, not a perp. And no one talks like that.

106
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:14,220
Yeah. No one talks like that.

107
00:07:14,470 --> 00:07:18,180
- Oh, what, like you're Mr. Cop?     - I'm more cop than you two.

108
00:07:18,430 --> 00:07:20,060
How do you figure that?

109
00:07:20,270 --> 00:07:22,520
I'm in the front seat, okay?

110
00:07:23,310 --> 00:07:25,610
I'm Gary's partner.

111
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:28,530
When you say "partner," it doesn't sound cop.

112
00:07:28,730 --> 00:07:30,740
It sounds gay.

113
00:07:31,530 --> 00:07:34,110
Um, jealous.

114
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:38,580
- Hey, we're undercover here.     - Oh, yeah. No problem.

115
00:07:39,790 --> 00:07:41,660
- Ross.     - Sorry.

116
00:07:42,830 --> 00:07:43,960
There.

117
00:07:47,090 --> 00:07:48,880
Hey, Gary. Who am I?

118
00:07:49,090 --> 00:07:50,760
Phone home.

119
00:07:54,090 --> 00:07:57,220
Look at Officer Ross riding back here with the visitors.

120
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:01,100
What's up with that, Serpico?

121
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:07,810
Are you thinking about me? No, of course you're not.

122
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:10,070
But if you are, call me tonight.

123
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:11,940
Okay, bye.

124
00:08:13,610 --> 00:08:15,740
No.

125
00:08:16,820 --> 00:08:18,660
I know.

126
00:08:19,660 --> 00:08:22,790
Thank God you were here. We have to erase that.

127
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:24,870
What? We can't do that.

128
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:27,170
We have to. What if Ross hears that...

129
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:29,500
...and calls her and they get back together?

130
00:08:29,750 --> 00:08:32,800
Is that what you want? Ross back with that controlling...

131
00:08:33,010 --> 00:08:36,430
...neurotic, crazy Emily who wouldn't let him see you?

132
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:38,720
No. Oh, no, no.

133
00:08:38,930 --> 00:08:41,560
God, no. He should not get back with her.

134
00:08:41,810 --> 00:08:45,310
I know that, you know that. Even Ross knows that.

135
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:47,810
But we have no right to erase his message.

136
00:08:48,060 --> 00:08:52,650
Look, I'm his sister and I love him. I don't want to see him get hurt.

137
00:08:52,900 --> 00:08:55,030
Doesn't that give me the right to control...

138
00:08:57,070 --> 00:08:58,660
Help him?

139
00:08:59,490 --> 00:09:01,830
He's not the one who needs help.

140
00:09:03,910 --> 00:09:05,660
She's obviously unstable.

141
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:09,290
She's thinking about running out on her wedding day.

142
00:09:13,050 --> 00:09:16,840
Okay, fine. But look at the position she's putting him in.

143
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:18,970
And what's he gonna do?

144
00:09:19,180 --> 00:09:22,260
Break up their marriage on their wedding day?

145
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:24,350
Who would do that?

146
00:09:28,020 --> 00:09:31,610
Okay, fine. All right. But that was different.

147
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:35,150
Although it did involve a lot of the same people.

148
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:38,910
This is some twisted joke she's playing on him.

149
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:42,240
You are crazy. She sounded genuinely upset.

150
00:09:42,450 --> 00:09:43,740
I mean, listen.

151
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,250
Your messages have been erased.

152
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:49,460
No.

153
00:09:51,790 --> 00:09:55,590
Okay, but we're safe, right? Nothing bad's gonna go down.

154
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:58,130
No. But that reminds me. Sign this.

155
00:09:58,380 --> 00:09:59,470
What is it?

156
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:02,390
It says you can't sue if you scrape your knee...

157
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:04,220
...or get your head blown off.

158
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:08,730
Oh, hurry up. I want to sign that.

159
00:10:09,810 --> 00:10:10,810
Here he comes.

160
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:14,650
What is he doing? What the hell is he doing?

161
00:10:14,900 --> 00:10:15,900
What is it?

162
00:10:16,070 --> 00:10:17,530
- Is everything okay?     - What?

163
00:10:17,740 --> 00:10:21,070
He sees us. Don't move. And don't look at him.

164
00:10:36,340 --> 00:10:39,340
Hey, it's okay. It was just a car backfire.

165
00:10:40,470 --> 00:10:43,180
Hey, look at that. You tried to save your buddy.

166
00:10:44,430 --> 00:10:45,560
You see that?

167
00:10:45,850 --> 00:10:47,520
You see what he did?

168
00:10:48,180 --> 00:10:49,600
You okay, man?

169
00:10:50,730 --> 00:10:52,310
Uh-huh.

170
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:54,520
Thanks, Joey.

171
00:10:56,440 --> 00:10:58,820
Uh... Hello?

172
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,490
Hi.

173
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,080
We should go.

174
00:11:10,250 --> 00:11:11,250
No, wait.

175
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:12,540
Oh, yeah. Right.

176
00:11:12,920 --> 00:11:14,880
No. Monica.

177
00:11:15,460 --> 00:11:17,300
Monica, we have to fix this.

178
00:11:17,550 --> 00:11:19,670
What can we do? You erased the message.

179
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:21,420
Unless we tell him.

180
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:25,010
If you want to be rational, I can't argue with you.

181
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:26,720
All right?

182
00:11:27,010 --> 00:11:30,390
Fine, tell him. I just don't want to be a part of it.

183
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:35,480
Maybe that's Emily leaving the exact same message.

184
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:38,940
Hey, Ross, it's you.

185
00:11:39,110 --> 00:11:41,190
I just want you to remember this feeling.

186
00:11:41,820 --> 00:11:44,450
You are lucky to be alive.

187
00:11:44,660 --> 00:11:47,910
So live every day to the fullest.

188
00:11:48,160 --> 00:11:51,080
Love yourself, okay?

189
00:11:51,620 --> 00:11:53,620
And also get stamps. Bye.

190
00:11:55,330 --> 00:11:58,840
Play that message for Emily, and this problem goes away.

191
00:11:59,090 --> 00:12:00,130
Right?

192
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:03,550
Anybody want to meet a hero?

193
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:05,930
John Glenn is here?

194
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:07,640
No. Joey.

195
00:12:07,890 --> 00:12:10,140
We had the most incredible night.

196
00:12:10,350 --> 00:12:12,600
- We're in the car...     - Wait. Hold on.

197
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:16,480
- Hi.     - Hi.

198
00:12:16,650 --> 00:12:18,440
Okay, go ahead.

199
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:23,030
So we're in the car, and bang. A shot was fired.

200
00:12:23,490 --> 00:12:26,780
And Joey, with no regard for his own safety...

201
00:12:27,030 --> 00:12:29,080
...throws himself on me.

202
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:30,370
My God.

203
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:33,120
It was a car backfire.

204
00:12:33,330 --> 00:12:34,830
But he didn't know that.

205
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:36,710
Yeah, I didn't know that.

206
00:12:38,710 --> 00:12:41,670
It could just as easily have been a bullet.

207
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:44,920
Ever think about joining the force? We could use a guy like you.

208
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:47,220
Who jumps at loud noises.

209
00:12:49,180 --> 00:12:52,220
Wow. I could have died tonight.

210
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:55,310
If the car that backfired had run over you.

211
00:12:56,940 --> 00:13:00,820
I'm going before he starts rambling about his newfound respect for life.

212
00:13:01,070 --> 00:13:04,740
I do have a newfound respect for life.

213
00:13:05,950 --> 00:13:07,780
Oh, my God.

214
00:13:10,330 --> 00:13:13,500
- You want to get some dinner?     - Yeah, sure.

215
00:13:13,660 --> 00:13:18,500
You know what? If I heard a shot right now, I'd throw my body on you.

216
00:13:18,750 --> 00:13:21,340
Maybe we should walk in a bad neighborhood.

217
00:13:21,590 --> 00:13:22,880
Okay.

218
00:13:24,380 --> 00:13:26,800
- Bye.     - Bye.

219
00:13:30,810 --> 00:13:32,470
Cut it out.

220
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:36,430
I'd hate to save your life and kick your ass on the same day.

221
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:46,490
Dude.

222
00:13:47,150 --> 00:13:48,150
Why'd you take off?

223
00:13:48,530 --> 00:13:50,620
Just going for a walk.

224
00:13:51,330 --> 00:13:53,330
Around the living room, whatever.

225
00:13:54,450 --> 00:13:57,910
- Is something wrong?     - No. No, I'm just tired.

226
00:13:58,120 --> 00:14:00,420
You know, from the walk.

227
00:14:01,710 --> 00:14:02,710
Okay.

228
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:05,000
You dove in front of Ross.

229
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:07,340
Ross.

230
00:14:08,010 --> 00:14:09,970
That's what this is about.

231
00:14:12,050 --> 00:14:14,810
Oh, my God. You hate Ross.

232
00:14:16,060 --> 00:14:17,180
I don't hate Ross.

233
00:14:17,390 --> 00:14:21,190
Of course you do. I saved him. You're mad at me. It adds up.

234
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:23,980
You want Ross out of the picture.

235
00:14:24,730 --> 00:14:25,730
What picture?

236
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:28,570
I don't know. But I don't like what I'm hearing.

237
00:14:28,990 --> 00:14:32,740
I'm glad you saved Ross. But it could've been a bullet.

238
00:14:32,990 --> 00:14:35,200
And you didn't try to save me.

239
00:14:35,740 --> 00:14:37,040
Oh.

240
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:40,460
You're upset because you think I chose Ross over you.

241
00:14:40,670 --> 00:14:45,170
No, I knew you could take care of yourself.

242
00:14:45,340 --> 00:14:49,300
You know? I mean, Ross needs help. He's not "street" like us.

243
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:53,140
You'd risk your life for Ross before you would for me.

244
00:14:53,350 --> 00:14:55,010
That's the bottom line.

245
00:14:56,390 --> 00:14:57,970
No, not exactly.

246
00:14:58,560 --> 00:14:59,810
All right, look.

247
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:03,020
I wasn't trying to save Ross.

248
00:15:03,900 --> 00:15:05,060
Okay?

249
00:15:06,190 --> 00:15:08,820
My sandwich was next to Ross.

250
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:12,240
All right?

251
00:15:13,570 --> 00:15:16,330
I was trying to save my sandwich.

252
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:19,950
From a bullet?

253
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:24,170
- I know it doesn't make much sense.   - "Much" sense?

254
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:27,670
Chandler, it was instinct. I just went for it.

255
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:30,340
You risked your life for a sandwich?

256
00:15:30,550 --> 00:15:32,590
I know it sounds crazy...

257
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:37,310
...but this is the greatest sandwich in the world.

258
00:15:39,430 --> 00:15:42,190
So you didn't choose Ross before me?

259
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:44,900
No. I would never do that.

260
00:15:45,150 --> 00:15:47,020
You're like my brother.

261
00:15:47,900 --> 00:15:49,980
- Really?     - Yeah.

262
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:54,700
In fact, to prove how much you mean to me...

263
00:15:59,370 --> 00:16:00,370
Here.

264
00:16:01,410 --> 00:16:04,120
- Thanks.     - Easy, it's not a hot dog.

265
00:16:10,380 --> 00:16:12,090
How good is that?

266
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:14,050
Oh, yeah.

267
00:16:14,890 --> 00:16:16,180
See?

268
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:17,640
What are you doing?

269
00:16:19,390 --> 00:16:21,600
You're showing me how much I mean to you.

270
00:16:21,810 --> 00:16:23,180
With a bite.

271
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:25,440
Jeez.

272
00:16:41,750 --> 00:16:43,000
Hi.

273
00:16:43,910 --> 00:16:45,500
What are you doing here?

274
00:16:45,710 --> 00:16:47,000
Hey, you know what?

275
00:16:47,210 --> 00:16:49,540
You are in our apartment all the time.

276
00:16:49,750 --> 00:16:52,260
This is just a drop in the bucket, mister.

277
00:16:54,130 --> 00:16:58,300
It doesn't matter. The important thing is that you're here.

278
00:16:58,550 --> 00:17:02,100
You're my friend and you're here.

279
00:17:07,310 --> 00:17:10,190
Okay, just a little scared. What's going on?

280
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:12,900
The most amazing thing happened tonight.

281
00:17:13,110 --> 00:17:15,450
I thought my number was up.

282
00:17:15,700 --> 00:17:18,570
I had an actual near-death experience.

283
00:17:18,820 --> 00:17:20,030
What happened?

284
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:24,700
We were on the ride-along with Gary and somebody took a shot at me.

285
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,130
Really?

286
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:31,460
No. A car backfired.

287
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:37,930
But I thought somebody was taking a shot at me. And, Rach...

288
00:17:38,090 --> 00:17:39,640
...I survived.

289
00:17:41,430 --> 00:17:45,480
And I was filled with this great respect for life.

290
00:17:45,730 --> 00:17:47,980
I want to experience every moment.

291
00:17:48,230 --> 00:17:51,480
I want to seize every opportunity.

292
00:17:51,690 --> 00:17:55,360
I am seeing everything so clearly now.

293
00:17:55,610 --> 00:17:57,740
Because a car backfired?

294
00:17:58,450 --> 00:18:00,450
Okay. Why are you here?

295
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:06,330
I don't know how this fits into your whole seizing thing...

296
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:08,160
...but Emily called you today.

297
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:11,710
- You talked to her?     - She left a message.

298
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:13,840
But it kind of got erased.

299
00:18:14,090 --> 00:18:17,590
I mean, there's something wrong with your machine.

300
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:19,220
What did she say?

301
00:18:19,890 --> 00:18:23,810
Something about having second thoughts about the wedding.

302
00:18:24,010 --> 00:18:27,060
And did you guys make a mistake breaking up?

303
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:29,730
And she wants you to call her.

304
00:18:30,650 --> 00:18:31,650
Wow.

305
00:18:32,110 --> 00:18:35,020
That was a good thing that I told you, right?

306
00:18:35,860 --> 00:18:37,690
Yeah. Yes. Of course.

307
00:18:37,950 --> 00:18:40,950
Okay, thank you. Thank you. Because...

308
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:43,620
I'm gonna tell Monica I was right.

309
00:18:43,830 --> 00:18:45,540
Because she didn't want...

310
00:18:45,740 --> 00:18:50,290
Not important. Point is, I was right. Your decision.

311
00:18:50,460 --> 00:18:51,460
Okay?

312
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:52,920
I was right.

313
00:18:53,170 --> 00:18:54,920
Your decision.

314
00:18:55,170 --> 00:18:56,630
Right.

315
00:18:56,840 --> 00:18:59,090
I guess I should call Emily.

316
00:18:59,340 --> 00:19:01,590
No, that's not the right decision.

317
00:19:01,840 --> 00:19:03,300
That's not right.

318
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:04,800
Ross, come on.

319
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:06,640
I mean...

320
00:19:06,930 --> 00:19:08,890
...that woman made you miserable.

321
00:19:09,640 --> 00:19:10,640
Okay, Ross?

322
00:19:10,850 --> 00:19:13,400
Do you really want to get back into that?

323
00:19:15,070 --> 00:19:16,820
Okay, look. Yesterday...

324
00:19:17,070 --> 00:19:20,190
...I wouldn't have even considered calling her back.

325
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:22,910
But my ex-wife calls on the same day...

326
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:25,580
...I have a near-death experience?

327
00:19:25,830 --> 00:19:27,830
That's gotta mean something.

328
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:32,960
That was not a near-death experience. That was barely an experience.

329
00:19:33,330 --> 00:19:35,330
You weren't there.

330
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:40,840
Maybe this is something that I'm supposed to seize, you know?

331
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:44,050
Okay. You know what?

332
00:19:44,300 --> 00:19:48,100
Maybe this is not about seizing stuff.

333
00:19:48,350 --> 00:19:51,890
Maybe this is about escaping stuff.

334
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:53,940
Okay? Look at today.

335
00:19:54,190 --> 00:19:55,730
I mean, you escaped...

336
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:57,440
...death.

337
00:19:59,610 --> 00:20:02,860
And maybe this is a chance for you to escape...

338
00:20:03,110 --> 00:20:05,030
...getting back together with Emily.

339
00:20:06,450 --> 00:20:07,990
That does make sense.

340
00:20:09,790 --> 00:20:13,540
Because I do want to seize some opportunity...

341
00:20:13,790 --> 00:20:17,380
...but I really don't want to see or talk to her.

342
00:20:19,170 --> 00:20:21,670
Well, there you go.

343
00:20:22,420 --> 00:20:24,180
Yeah, maybe today's just...

344
00:20:25,010 --> 00:20:27,180
...close-call day.

345
00:20:29,560 --> 00:20:31,390
Hey, thanks, Rach.

346
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:33,270
Oh, honey. No problem.

347
00:20:34,350 --> 00:20:36,980
Wait, wait. The message is blinking.

348
00:20:37,310 --> 00:20:39,110
Maybe you didn't erase it.

349
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:41,820
Hey, Ross, it's you...

350
00:20:42,440 --> 00:20:46,610
That's an old message. Nobody needs to hear that.

351
00:20:47,990 --> 00:20:50,080
Hey, um, was Monica here?

352
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:51,540
Yeah.

353
00:20:51,700 --> 00:20:53,540
I want my money back.

354
00:20:54,620 --> 00:20:57,040
You probably need that for stamps, right?

355
00:21:05,050 --> 00:21:06,050
Hey, Pheebs?

356
00:21:06,220 --> 00:21:08,010
Has Gary ever been shot at for real?

357
00:21:08,220 --> 00:21:09,350
Yes, once.

358
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:11,600
A little.

359
00:21:11,810 --> 00:21:14,060
He kind of did it to himself.

360
00:21:14,730 --> 00:21:16,770
It's not really a good story.

361
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:21,110
I wonder how I'd react under fire. And not backfire...

362
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:22,860
...but heavy fire.

363
00:21:23,110 --> 00:21:25,110
Like if I was in a war.

364
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:27,240
Man, I would be great in a war.

365
00:21:27,490 --> 00:21:30,450
I think I'd make a fantastic military leader.

366
00:21:30,700 --> 00:21:34,290
I mean, I know I'd make general before any of you guys.

367
00:21:34,790 --> 00:21:38,040
Before or after you were shot by your own troops?

368
00:21:38,580 --> 00:21:42,340
I know Joey would be in the foxhole protecting all of us.

369
00:21:42,590 --> 00:21:45,340
If the foxhole was lined with sandwiches.

370
00:21:46,630 --> 00:21:48,840
Yeah, hero sandwiches.

371
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:55,810
You all know I'm a pacifist, so I'm not interested in war in any way.

372
00:21:56,060 --> 00:21:59,350
But when the revolution comes, I'll have to destroy you all.

373
00:22:00,560 --> 00:22:01,860
Not you, Joey.

